  "body": "## Goal\n\nStep 1, PR F1 of the UI plan #4245, for #3025. Add one Settings window for the per-user application settings. The answers on #3025 (comment of 2026-11-28) are the design.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A separate window (not a dock panel). It opens from the existing Settings button in the ribbon top band (#2428, `settings_drop.rs`; the button opens the window instead of the one-row dropdown) and from a \"Settings…\" row in the menu bar of PR E (#4490).\n- Settings apply at once. Each section has \"Reset to defaults\". The settings stay per-user (`prefs.json`, `view.json`), outside the project file and the undo history (#877).\n- Sections in this PR:\n  1. **Appearance:** theme and colour vision (the Theme door stays as a quick switch and can open this section).\n  2. **Graphics:** line width and anti-aliasing. They move here from the viewport Display menu (group \"Graphics\", #2818, `display_menu.rs`); remove that group there.\n  3. **Graphics device (read-only):** the adapter and the backend that the app uses (`gpu_line`) and the sample counts that the device offers.\n  4. **Updates:** \"Check for updates\" moves here from the Settings dropdown.\n- Rows use the form helpers (#1122). Components that hold no shell state go in `crates/ui-kit`.\n- No MCP tool and no CLI flag (answer 4 on #3025).\n\n## Done means\n\n- The window opens from the Settings button and from the menu bar. Each section's control changes its setting at once and writes the per-user file. \"Reset to defaults\" restores each section.\n- The Display menu no longer has the Graphics group. The Settings dropdown is gone (the button opens the window).\n- An old `prefs.json` / `view.json` loads with the same values as before.\n- Tests: open from both places, each control, reset, persistence, an old prefs file. A new layout test `layout_window_settings`. Updated layout and structural tests for the Display menu and the ribbon top band. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down (#1953). No snapshot PNG changes.\n- Before and after screenshots at 1366×768.\n- No change to toolpaths, posts or the project file.\n\nStacked on PR #4490 (PR E) for the menu-bar row. Part of #3025 and #4245.\n",
